request: Make the output easier to read. --behaviour

governor turn 1: ask  ("Easier to read" could mean several different output changes, and each would need a different test. Right now `todo list` prints only "[ ] title" lines. It leaves out the ids (which `todo complete` needs) and the due dates. I need to know which changes you want before I can write a test that checks them.)
governor asks: "Easier to read" could mean several things. Which of these do you want? Pick any combination, or describe something else.
(a) Show each todo's id, e.g. "#1 [ ] buy milk". You currently can't see the ids that `todo complete` needs.
(b) Show the due date when there is one, e.g. "#1 [ ] buy milk (due 2026-11-01)".
(c) Line up the columns so titles and due dates sit one under another.
(d) Sort the list, e.g. open todos first and then by due date.
(e) Add a summary line, e.g. "2 open, 1 done".
(f) Add terminal colours or symbols, such as ✓ for done.
(g) Make the messages from add, complete and errors more detailed, e.g. "Added #1: buy milk (due 2026-11-01)".
If you're happy with my default, I'll do (a) and (b) with the exact format "#<id> [ ] <title>" plus " (due YYYY-MM-DD)" when a due date is set. Everything else stays the same.

